SUMMARY:Gathering: A Collaborative Nature Art Experience for the Cancer Community
DESCRIPTION:Offered in collaboration with Dr. Kristin Huang\, a clinical psychologist and cancer survivor whose work explores the intersections of psychology\, creativity\, nature and human development. \nJoin us at Duke Gardens for an afternoon of creativity and connection for people whose lives have been touched by cancer. Using flowers\, leaves\, branches and other natural materials\, participants will create temporary designs on individual panels. There is no right way to make them\, and no art experience is needed. The invitation is simply to slow down\, work with the natural materials and create something that feels meaningful to you. Individual panels will be brought together in a large\, quilt-like installation\, transforming many distinct creations into a shared work of art. Weather permitting\, the completed installation will be assembled outdoors on the Gateway Gardens Event Lawn\, offering a chance to step back and experience what we have created together. Gathering is less about making something permanent than about the experience of making: noticing beauty\, experimenting\, reflecting and allowing space to discover what emerges. Each piece stands on its own while also becoming part of something larger—a fitting expression of the individuality and shared connection within the cancer community. All materials will be provided. No art experience is necessary. \nFee: Free; registration recommended. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Meet at the Barnes Welcome Center \nAccessibility: This program takes place indoors and outdoors\, in areas accessible via paved paths\, with accessible restrooms available nearby. Please note that program supplies include natural plant materials.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/gathering-a-collaborative-nature-art-experience-for-the-cancer-community/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
